---
description: >-
  Class diagram under the dagre layout with `class.hierarchicalNamespaces`
  set to false, testing compact (flat) namespace rendering instead of
  nested namespace boxes, using dot-notation namespace names
  (Company.Engineering.Backend, Company.Engineering.Frontend, Company) and
  cross-namespace relationships from a CEO class.
config:
  layout: dagre
  class:
    hierarchicalNamespaces: false
---
classDiagram
  namespace Company.Engineering.Backend {
  class Developer {
    +writeCode()
  }
  }
  namespace Company.Engineering.Frontend {
  class Designer {
    +createMockup()
  }
  }
  namespace Company {
  class CEO {
    +makeDecisions()
  }
  }
  CEO --> Developer : oversees
  CEO --> Designer : oversees

---
description: >-
  Dagre-layout class diagram using dot-notation namespace names to express
  nesting (Company.Engineering.Backend, Company.Engineering.Frontend,
  Company.Engineering) with a TechLead class in the parent namespace
  leading classes declared in the two child namespaces.
config:
  logLevel: 1
  htmlLabels: true
  layout: dagre
---
classDiagram
  namespace Company.Engineering.Backend {
  class Developer {
    +writeCode()
  }
  }
  namespace Company.Engineering.Frontend {
  class Designer {
    +createMockup()
  }
  }
  namespace Company.Engineering {
  class TechLead {
    +planSprint()
  }
  }
  TechLead --> Developer : leads
  TechLead --> Designer : leads

---
description: >-
  Dagre-layout class diagram where namespaces are nested syntactically
  (namespace blocks written inside another namespace block, e.g.
  `namespace Platform { namespace Auth {...} namespace Data {...} }`)
  rather than via dot-notation, with a Gateway class delegating to classes
  in each nested namespace.
config:
  logLevel: 1
  htmlLabels: true
  layout: dagre
---
classDiagram
  namespace Platform {
  namespace Auth {
    class UserService {
      +login()
      +logout()
    }
  }
  namespace Data {
    class Repository {
      +find()
      +save()
    }
  }
  class Gateway {
    +route()
  }
  }
  Gateway --> UserService : delegates
  Gateway --> Repository : delegates

